cal, biotechnology, and medical device industries; and development plan design, coordinated central laboratory, project management, regulatory affairs, clinical monitoring, data management and analysis, pharmacovigilance new drug application submissions, and post-marketing clinical support services. In addition, the company offers bio-analytical laboratory services, clinical human pharmacology, imaging services, and electrocardiography reading support for clinical trials. Medpace Holdings, Inc. was founded in 1992 and is based in Cincinnati, Ohio.","ceo_bio":"Dr. August James Troendle M.D. | CEO, President & Chairman | Age 69 | Compensation: $1.4M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 6K people. Revenue per employee of $383K ranks in the above the sector median among Healthcare peers, with revenue growing 22%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $103K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $5K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Medpace Holdings, Inc. is a large-cap healthcare business with a $18.3B market cap on $2.5B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +20% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 57% against a 11% cost of capital \u2014 a 46-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $682M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 27 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.58\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 5.0% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 19% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and within its sector the business captures 2.4\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 32% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 3 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.3229088141140683},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 6.2% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $140.3M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 22% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Healthcare peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 13% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (30.7% return)"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Is Medpace (MEDP) Stock Outpacing Its Medical Peers This Year?","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3029448/is-medpace-medp-stock-outpacing-its-medical-peers-this-year?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cyseop_template_1-3029448","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794577203.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Trading Systems Reacting to (MEDP) Volatility","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/35/Trading_Systems_Reacting_to_MEDP_Volatility_111226113002_1794501002.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794501002.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Medpace (MEDP) \u2013 Analysts\u2019 Weekly Ratings Changes","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/11/medpace-medp-analysts-weekly-ratings-changes.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794418010.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.077,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"3 Reasons Why Growth Investors Shouldn't Overlook Medpace (MEDP)","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3027933/3-reasons-why-growth-investors-shouldn-t-overlook-medpace-medp?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cyseop_template_11_growth-3027933","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794415501.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.382,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Is Medpace Holdings (MEDP) Fully Valued On Record Q3 Awards And Pipeline Growth?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/pharmaceuticals-biotech/nasdaq-medp/medpace-holdings/news/is-medpace-holdings-medp-fully-valued-on-re